#~ "`1.0` keeps the original cell, `0.9` shortens"
#~ " the selected axis by 10%, and `1.1` "
#~ "lengthens it by 10%. For near-equilibrium "
#~ "response, `0.95-1.05` is usually sufficient. A "
#~ "bcc/fcc/fct study may extend to `0.7-1.4`, but"
#~ " check nearest-neighbor distances and volumes "
#~ "in every batch before committing DFT "
#~ "resources."

